any roads  bridges rail lines will all need  repairing and replacing  the 2002 flood on the elba and the  danube rivers ran up a bill of around 13  billion euros in germany  the rebuilding this time may well cost  much more  amid criticisms about the failure of  warning systems  and the speed of the emergency response  one thing the political leaders can do  is direct money to where it is so  urgently needed  all right let's check in with an our  reporter now benjamin alvarez-gruber  he's on the ground  covering the latest developments in the  town of badminster ifa  benjamin there are now also fears of  coronavirus spreading faster  how are health authorities responding to  that threat  that's right sumi we are not in  badminton alpha we were there yesterday  today we are in avila one of the worst  hit  is cities in the state of  rhineland-palatinate where local  authorities and state authorities fear  that the areas affected by the floods  might also  become a super spreader event so they  brought  a mobile vaccination center it's a bus  that you can see here right behind me  where not only residents but also  volunteers can come here  to get their job without an appointment  yesterday there was the first day of  this bus more than 260 people  got the jab here and there will be also  teams going to the emergency shelters  where local authorities fear  that their risk of getting infected with  corvette 19 is especially high  dozens and dozens of people in the area  are still unaccounted for so what can  you tell us at this point about rescue  efforts where you are  rescue efforts continue around the clock  there are several groups involved  there is on one side police there are  also soldiers that have been deployed to  the area  and the civil emergency organization is  also hearing a lot of volunteers  we spoke to firefighters and they told  us that they are still trying to pump  water out of houses  and of underground parking lots where  many well some people are